.TH SYSFORGE "1" "2026\-04\-18" "sysforge" "Generated Python Manual"
.SH NAME
sysforge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysforge
[-h] [-v] COMMAND ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Arch Linux AUR helper with compiler\-optimized builds.

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,build\/\fR
Build a package from a PKGBUILD.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,fetch\/\fR
Download PKGBUILD(s) into pkgbuild_src_dir without building.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,update\/\fR
Check for and rebuild outdated sysforge\-managed packages.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,resolve\/\fR
Show which profile would be applied to a package and why.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,converge\/\fR
Detect and repair packages whose build flags have drifted from the current profile.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,doctor\/\fR
Health\-check installed package depends + shared\-library linkage.
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,packages\/\fR
Manage packages.toml (list, add, remove, sync).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,run\/\fR
Execute a pipeline stage (pipeline, hardware, reconfigure, toolchain, packages, kernel).
.TP
\fBsysforge\fR \fI\,setup\/\fR
Configure system integration (pacman IgnoreGroup for sf\-build).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge build'\/\fR
usage: sysforge build [\-h] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS] [\-\-interactive] [\-\-persist\-log]
                      [\-\-no\-pkg\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]
                      [\-\-cc COMPILER] [\-\-cxx COMPILER] [\-\-ld LINKER]
                      [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-no\-update]
                      [\-\-cleansrc] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-track\-deps]
                      PKGBUILD [PKGBUILD ...]

.TP
\fBPKGBUILD\fR
One or more packages to build (path, directory, or bare package name).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge build'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Additional makepkg flags, appended after profile makepkg_flags. Combined short
flags are expanded: \-sfci becomes \-s \-f \-c \-i. Example: sysforge build
PKGBUILD \-m '\-sfci'

.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Strip \-\-noconfirm from profile makepkg_flags.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep the per\-package log file after a successful build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable the per\-package log file.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for the per\-package log file (default: alongside the PKGBUILD).

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cc\fR \fI\,COMPILER\/\fR
Override CC (C compiler) for this build, e.g. \-\-cc clang.

.TP
\fB\-\-cxx\fR \fI\,COMPILER\/\fR
Override CXX (C++ compiler) for this build, e.g. \-\-cxx clang++.

.TP
\fB\-\-ld\fR \fI\,LINKER\/\fR
Override linker for this build, e.g. \-\-ld lld.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary (ccache/sccache hit rates) after the build.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before building.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge the package src dir and re\-clone before building. Refuses (per package)
if the existing clone has uncommitted changes, unpushed commits, or no
upstream tracking branch.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-track\-deps\fR
Auto\-add resolved AUR dependencies to packages.toml with reason='dependency'.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge fetch'\/\fR
usage: sysforge fetch [\-h] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] PKG [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more package names to download.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge fetch'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase for packages that are already cloned.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
usage: sysforge update [\-h] [\-\-all] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-devel] [\-\-offline]
                       [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                       [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-no\-pkg\-log]
                       [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS]
                       [\-\-interactive] [\-\-no\-cleanbuild] [\-\-cleansrc]
                       [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Limit update to these package names (default: all sysforge\-managed packages).

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge update'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Also discover foreign packages (pacman \-Qm) not yet tracked; add to
packages.toml and rebuild if outdated.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be rebuilt without doing it.

.TP
\fB\-\-devel\fR
Include VCS packages (\-git, \-svn, \-hg, \-bzr) in the rebuild.

.TP
\fB\-\-offline\fR
No network: skip git pulls, clones, and AUR RPC. Pure local version check.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml for \-\-all discovery (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Extra flags passed verbatim to makepkg (e.g. \-m '\-f' to force rebuild).
Combined short flags are expanded: \-sfci becomes \-s \-f \-c \-i.

.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Pause on build failures to allow manual correction (default: log failure and
continue).

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cleanbuild\fR
Skip the automatic \-\-cleanbuild (\-C) added for update runs. Useful when
packages are already built and you only need to re\-run the install step.

.TP
\fB\-\-cleansrc\fR
Purge each package's src dir and re\-clone before building. Per\-package fatal
if the clone has uncommitted changes, unpushed commits, or no upstream — that
package is reported failed and the run continues.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge resolve'\/\fR
usage: sysforge resolve [\-h] [\-\-show\-flags | \-\-deps] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] PKG

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Path to a PKGBUILD file, or bare package name.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge resolve'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-flags\fR
Print the full resolved flag set.

.TP
\fB\-\-deps\fR
Show transitive dependency tree with build order instead of profile info.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge converge'\/\fR
usage: sysforge converge [\-h] [\-\-apply] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                         [\-\-profile\-conf FILE] [\-\-no\-pkg\-log] [\-\-persist\-log]
                         [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS] [\-\-cache\-report]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge converge'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Rebuild all DRIFTED packages with the current profile.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-log\fR
Disable per\-package log files (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for per\-package log files (only relevant with \-\-apply).

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Extra flags passed to makepkg during \-\-apply rebuilds (e.g. \-m '\-C' to
cleanbuild). \-f is always injected automatically.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after \-\-apply runs.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
usage: sysforge doctor [\-h] [\-\-graphics] [\-\-all] [\-\-repo] [\-\-shallow]
                       [\-\-quiet] [\-\-suggest]
                       [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more installed package names to verify. Without any
PKG/\-\-graphics/\-\-all, the command exits with usage.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge doctor'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-graphics\fR
Expand to the graphics stack (mesa, vulkan, libglvnd, wayland, libdrm, libva,
libvdpau, egl\-wayland, xwayland, gamescope, plus per\-vendor drivers from the
hardware overlay's gpu_vendors) AND run system\-state probes (nvidia\-drm
modeset, driver version skew, Wayland explicit\-sync protocol, Steam GPU accel,
session type).

.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Verify every installed package — foreign and non\-foreign (pacman \-Q). Slow but
comprehensive.

.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR
Verify every non\-foreign (native repo) package. Narrower than \-\-all.

.TP
\fB\-\-shallow\fR
Do not recurse into transitive dependencies of each target.

.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Suppress clean lines; print only packages with issues.

.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR, \fB\-s\fR
For each unsatisfied soname, look up candidate packages via `pacman \-Fq`.
Findings split into 'install candidates' (missing from disk — install the
package) and 'ABI\-drift candidates' (present but one of their versioned
symbols no longer resolves — rebuild or upgrade, not reinstall). Requires a
synced files db (`sudo pacman \-Fy`).

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-state] [\-\-diagnose]
                         [\-\-problems\-only] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                         {list,add,remove,sync,repair\-state} ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,list\/\fR
Show packages in packages.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,add\/\fR
Add a package: classify source, infer pkgbuild_patch, append entry.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,remove\/\fR
Remove a package entry.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,sync\/\fR
Re\-validate inferable fields (source, pkgbuild_patch) for all entries.
.TP
\fBsysforge packages\fR \fI\,repair\-state\/\fR
Re\-parse PKGBUILDs to rewrite build_state.toml entries that contain unexpanded shell variables (e.g. '$_pkgname\-git').

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages list'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages list [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-state] [\-\-diagnose]
                              [\-\-problems\-only] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages list'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR
List build_state.toml entries instead of packages.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-diagnose\fR
Per\-package directory/git status as `sysforge update` would see it.

.TP
\fB\-\-problems\-only\fR
With \-\-diagnose: show only packages that would silently fail.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages add'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages add [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] PKG [PKG ...]

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
One or more package names to add.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages add'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages remove'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages remove [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] PKG

.TP
\fBPKG\fR
Package name to remove.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages remove'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages sync'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages sync [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-dry\-run]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages sync'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would change without writing.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge packages repair\-state'\/\fR
usage: sysforge packages repair\-state [\-h] [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-dry\-run]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages repair\-state'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show the planned repair without writing.

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR
List build_state.toml entries instead of packages.toml.

.TP
\fB\-\-diagnose\fR
Per\-package directory/git status as `sysforge update` would see it.

.TP
\fB\-\-problems\-only\fR
With \-\-diagnose: show only packages that would silently fail.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory for build_state.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run [\-h] STAGE ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'sysforge run'\/\fR
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,pipeline\/\fR
Run the full install pipeline (stages 1–8).
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,hardware\/\fR
Re\-run hardware detection and refresh hardware_profile.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,reconfigure\/\fR
Pre\-build checkpoint: review configs, disk, network, GPG, build preview.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,toolchain\/\fR
Build and install the LLVM/GCC toolchain from toolchain.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,packages\/\fR
Build and install non\-kernel packages from packages.toml.
.TP
\fBsysforge run\fR \fI\,kernel\/\fR
Build and install the custom kernel configured in kernel.toml.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run pipeline'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run pipeline [\-h] [\-\-resume] [\-\-start\-from STAGE]
                             [\-\-force\-retry] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-packages FILE]
                             [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-no\-unified\-log]
                             [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-purge\-log]
                             [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]
                             [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-no\-update]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run pipeline'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR
Resume from the last checkpoint.

.TP
\fB\-\-start\-from\fR \fI\,STAGE\/\fR
Start from this stage, marking all prior stages as skipped. Useful on a live
system: \-\-start\-from reconfigure

.TP
\fB\-\-force\-retry\fR
Retry all failed packages without prompting.

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-unified\-log\fR
Disable the unified log file.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-purge\-log\fR
Truncate the unified log before this run.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the pipeline completes.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run hardware'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run hardware [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run hardware'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be written without writing.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run reconfigure'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run reconfigure [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-packages FILE]
                                [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run reconfigure'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Run all steps non\-interactively without writing any changes.

.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (used by disk and preview steps).

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run toolchain'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run toolchain [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-makepkg FLAGS]
                              [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-cache\-report] [\-\-abi\-check]
                              [\-\-state\-dir DIR] [\-\-rebuild\-profdata]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run toolchain'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-makepkg\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR, \fB\-m\fR \fI\,FLAGS\/\fR
Additional makepkg flags appended to each build. Example: \-m '\-f' to force
rebuild of already\-built packages. Install flags (\-i/\-\-install) are ignored;
the toolchain controls which passes install to the system.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-rebuild\-profdata\fR
Force a full 3\-pass PGO build even if compatible profdata already exists.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run packages'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run packages [\-h] [\-\-packages FILE] [\-\-dry\-run]
                             [\-\-force\-retry] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs]
                             [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-cache\-report]
                             [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]
                             [\-\-profile\-conf FILE]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run packages'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-packages\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to packages.toml (default:
/home/keith/src/sysforge/tests/data/etc/sysforge/packages.toml).

.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-force\-retry\fR
Retry all failed packages without prompting.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to a flag_profiles.toml to use instead of the default.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge run kernel'\/\fR
usage: sysforge run kernel [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-no\-update] [\-\-no\-pkg\-logs]
                           [\-\-persist\-log] [\-\-log\-dir DIR] [\-\-cache\-report]
                           [\-\-abi\-check] [\-\-state\-dir DIR]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge run kernel'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would run without executing anything.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\fR
Skip git pull \-\-rebase before each build.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pkg\-logs\fR
Disable per\-package log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-persist\-log\fR
Keep log files after successful completion.

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Directory for log files.

.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-report\fR
Print a structured cache summary after the run.

.TP
\fB\-\-abi\-check\fR
Run a post\-build ABI compatibility check on built shared libraries.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Override state directory.

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'sysforge setup'\/\fR
usage: sysforge setup [\-h] [\-\-pacman\-conf FILE]

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'sysforge setup'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-pacman\-conf\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Path to pacman.conf (default: /etc/pacman.conf).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbosity level. Default: errors only. \-v adds warnings. \-vv adds
informational messages. \-vvv adds debug output.

